member.summary:
            Materials round, stage 0 (diagnostic): writes a plain-text report of every material in the model and its
            loaded links. The report covers:


how many elements use each material;

its shading colour and its appearance asset's schema;

a full dump of the asset's properties, including connected texture assets;

where each bitmap was found (or not), and whether its path looks Autodesk-supplied;

image formats and sizes, and an estimate of the embedded size at 512 / 1024 px;

what texture discovery found on this machine (library roots, registry, Revit.ini).

reflection probes round, stage 0: the reflection strength, roughness and tier of every used material
            (), the properties they came from, and the finish enum values seen.

            Read only, best effort: an unreadable material or property is noted in the report and the scan carries on.
            The report confirms the property names before the material extraction is written against them.
